  "id": "DrugBank_DB00741 - MONDO_2970",
  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Ciliary Body Disease through a chain of indications that link it to inflammatory conditions. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone may be associated with Iritis (uveitis), which in turn is linked to Fluorometholone and Medrysone, both of which are indicated to cause Ciliary Body Disease. This pathway highlights a potential role of corticosteroids in triggering inflammatory responses that contribute to ciliary body dysfunction. The overlapping indications across different paths suggest a possible mechanism involving inflammation and immune-mediated processes. While the direct causal link between Hydrocortisone and Ciliary Body Disease remains indirect, the cumulative evidence supports a role of corticosteroids in the development of this condition through their anti-inflammatory effects. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of corticosteroid use in the context of inflammatory diseases, with the ciliary body being a target of these effects.",
